@page "/employmentverification/verification"
@layout ConsoleLayout

@* The route registered as submenu 9 in ShareData/Auth/SubMenuList.cs, which is what
   the home application card is built from. It used to be the whole module; the console
   is now three tabs, so this stays as a redirect to the first of them rather than
   becoming a fourth page.

   Keeping it means the home card, any bookmark, and the backend application/submenu
   seed data (application 8, submenu 9) all keep working untouched - the feature guide
   requires those IDs to agree across the frontend catalogs and the API seed, so a
   renamed route here would be a much wider change than it looks.

   ConsoleLayout rather than EVLayout: rendering the navbar for the instant before the
   redirect fires would flash a shell the user never lands on. *@

<CibiLoaderComponent />

@code {
    [Inject] private NavigationManager Nav { get; set; } = default!;

    protected override void OnInitialized() =>
        Nav.NavigateTo(EmploymentVerificationRoutes.NeedsRequest, replace: true);
}
